  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Truxton_II",
  "canonical_title": "Truxton II",
  "description": "Dense Asteroid Mining Belts & Fortress Cores, Truxton II (Tatsujin Ou) (Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)). Truxton IIis a 1992 vertically scrolling shooter video game developed and published byToaplanforarcades. It is the sequel toTruxton, which was released in 1988 and later ported to various platforms. Truxton II later received a conversion to theFM TownsbyVingand published exclusively in Japan in April1993, featuring various changes from the original version.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Dense Asteroid Mining Belts & Fortress Cores' from Truxton II (Tatsujin Ou) (Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)). World brief: Dense Asteroid Mining Belts & Fortress Cores, Truxton II (Tatsujin Ou) (Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)). Truxton IIis a 1992 vertically scrolling shooter video game developed and published byToaplanforarcades. It is the sequel toTruxton, which was released in 1988 and later ported to various platforms. Truxton II later received a conversion to theFM TownsbyVingand published exclusively in Japan in April1993, featuring various changes from the original version. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Truxton IIis a 1992 vertically scrolling shooter video game developed and published byToaplanforarcades. It is the sequel toTruxton, which was released in 1988 and later ported to various platforms. Truxton II later received a conversion to theFM TownsbyVingand published exclusively in Japan in April1993, featuring various changes from the original version. Truxton IIreceived positive reception from critics since its initial arcade launch and later on the FM Towns, garnering praise for the detailed presentation, graphics and sound design, though some criticized the length and noted it to be a standard shoot 'em up title. Nevertheless, it has since gained a cult following and as of 2019, the rights to the title are owned byTatsujin, a company founded in 2017 by former Toaplan member Masahiro Yuge alongside many other Toaplan IPs.",
  "brief": "Dense Asteroid Mining Belts & Fortress Cores, Truxton II (Tatsujin Ou) (Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)). Truxton IIis a 1992 vertically scrolling shooter video game developed and published byToaplanforarcades. It is the sequel toTruxton, which was released in 1988 and later ported to various platforms. Truxton II later received a conversion to theFM TownsbyVingand published exclusively in Japan in April1993, featuring various changes from the original version.",
  "page_title": "Truxton II"
 },
 {
  "id": 971,
  "game": "Batsugun",
  "target": "Orbital Space Defense Rings, Subsea Hangars & Base Superstructures",
  "platform": "Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Batsugun/Gameplay",
  "canonical_title": "Batsugun/Gameplay",
  "description": "Orbital Space Defense Rings, Subsea Hangars & Base Superstructures, Batsugun (Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)). All that stands between Renoselva's military forces and world domination are the Skull Hornets: a squadron of fighter pilots led by Prince Olisis (a play on Osiris) Gladebaran, Renoselva's own son. On Epsilon Centauri Prime, a distant planet similar to Earth, a global takeover is set into motion. This plan is masterminded by King Renoselva Gladebaran, the seventh ruler of his direct line.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Orbital Space Defense Rings, Subsea Hangars & Base Superstructures' from Batsugun (Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)). The attached reference image is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Orbital Space Defense Rings, Subsea Hangars & Base Superstructures, Batsugun (Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)). All that stands between Renoselva's military forces and world domination are the Skull Hornets: a squadron of fighter pilots led by Prince Olisis (a play on Osiris) Gladebaran, Renoselva's own son. On Epsilon Centauri Prime, a distant planet similar to Earth, a global takeover is set into motion. This plan is masterminded by King Renoselva Gladebaran, the seventh ruler of his direct line. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "On Epsilon Centauri Prime, a distant planet similar to Earth, a global takeover is set into motion. This plan is masterminded by King Renoselva Gladebaran, the seventh ruler of his direct line. The Imperial Army successfully stages multiple coup d'\u00e9tats upon various countries of the planet, in less than two weeks. All that stands between Renoselva's military forces and world domination are the Skull Hornets: a squadron of fighter pilots led by Prince Olisis (a play on Osiris) Gladebaran, Renoselva's own son. The Skull Hornets utilize the most powerful submersible jets which the planet's scientists have ever devised.",
  "brief": "Orbital Space Defense Rings, Subsea Hangars & Base Superstructures, Batsugun (Arcade (Psikyo / Toaplan / Raizing / Video System)). All that stands between Renoselva's military forces and world domination are the Skull Hornets: a squadron of fighter pilots led by Prince Olisis (a play on Osiris) Gladebaran, Renoselva's own son. On Epsilon Centauri Prime, a distant planet similar to Earth, a global takeover is set into motion. This plan is masterminded by King Renoselva Gladebaran, the seventh ruler of his direct line.",
  "page_title": "Batsugun",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null
 },
