  "description": "High-Rise Missile Facilities, Airport Runways & Subways, Elevator Action Returns (Arcade (Taito / Irem)). This game features far superior graphics, faster gameplay, and smoother controls. Elevator Action -Returns-(\u30a8\u30ec\u30d9\u30fc\u30bf\u30fc\u30a2\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3 \u30ea\u30bf\u30fc\u30f3\u30ba,Ereb\u0113t\u0101 Akushon Rit\u0101nzu?), known asElevator Action IIin North America, is a1994arcadegame byTaito. The enemies are also much tougher than they were in the original.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'High-Rise Missile Facilities, Airport Runways & Subways' from Elevator Action Returns (Arcade (Taito / Irem)). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: High-Rise Missile Facilities, Airport Runways & Subways, Elevator Action Returns (Arcade (Taito / Irem)). This game features far superior graphics, faster gameplay, and smoother controls. Elevator Action -Returns-(\u30a8\u30ec\u30d9\u30fc\u30bf\u30fc\u30a2\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3 \u30ea\u30bf\u30fc\u30f3\u30ba,Ereb\u0113t\u0101 Akushon Rit\u0101nzu?), known asElevator Action IIin North America, is a1994arcadegame byTaito. The enemies are also much tougher than they were in the original. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Elevator Action -Returns-(\u30a8\u30ec\u30d9\u30fc\u30bf\u30fc\u30a2\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3 \u30ea\u30bf\u30fc\u30f3\u30ba,Ereb\u0113t\u0101 Akushon Rit\u0101nzu?), known asElevator Action IIin North America, is a1994arcadegame byTaito. The game is the sequel to the arcade classicElevator Actionfrom1983. This game features far superior graphics, faster gameplay, and smoother controls. The enemies are also much tougher than they were in the original. Where the first game had a single secret agent stealing documents, this game has up to two players controlling one or two of three characters on a mission to defeat a band of terrorists armed with nuclear bombs. This was also the first game in the series to feature a full-fledged story with in-game cut scenes, with voice overs. Elevator Action Returns was ported to theSega Saturnin1997, with the original Elevator Action as an unlockable. The game was included as part ofTaito Legends 2for thePlayStation 2,PCandXboxin2006. The Saturn ve",
  "brief": "High-Rise Missile Facilities, Airport Runways & Subways, Elevator Action Returns (Arcade (Taito / Irem)). This game features far superior graphics, faster gameplay, and smoother controls. Elevator Action -Returns-(\u30a8\u30ec\u30d9\u30fc\u30bf\u30fc\u30a2\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3 \u30ea\u30bf\u30fc\u30f3\u30ba,Ereb\u0113t\u0101 Akushon Rit\u0101nzu?), known asElevator Action IIin North America, is a1994arcadegame byTaito. The enemies are also much tougher than they were in the original.",
